            <section>
               <title value="Hospital course note"/>
               <code>
                  <coding>
                     <system value="http://loinc.org"/>
                     <code value="8648-8"/>
                     <display value="Hospital course note"/>
                  </coding>
               </code>
               <text>
                  <status value="generated"/>
                  <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the recent hospital admission of your patient, a 74-year-old male, who presented on 07/02/2010 with an acute exacerbation of his known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD). On admission, he exhibited marked dyspnoea, increased sputum production, and reduced oxygen saturation. Chest X-ray confirmed pulmonary hyperinflation consistent with COPD. Arterial blood gas analysis revealed hypoxaemia with mild hypercapnia. Blood tests showed elevated inflammatory markers. He was treated with nebulised bronchodilators, systemic corticosteroids, supplemental oxygen therapy, and closely monitored with pulse oximetry and regular vital signs assessment. He responded well to treatment with significant symptomatic improvement. He was discharged on 08/02/2010 with a prescription for oral steroids and inhalers, and I would kindly ask you to arrange follow-up and consider pulmonary rehabilitation referral. Yours sincerely, Dr. [Hospital Physician]</div>
               </text>
            </section>
